<%# The spec asks for a remaining amount that is always visible, so it reads the
    same whether it is zero or not: the organizer should never have to wonder
    whether the line is missing or the figure is nil.

    In custom mode this is the number being worked down to zero, and SplitLogic
    updates it on every drag. Its own partial because a Turbo Stream redraws it
    whenever a row is added or removed. %>
<div id="remaining" class="mt-4 border-t-2 border-black pt-3">
  <p class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
    <span class="font-medium">Left to give</span>
    <span class="font-medium tabular-nums" data-split-logic-target="remaining">
      <%= money(split.remaining_cents) %>
    </span>
  </p>

  <% if split.custom? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-black/60">
      Every share has to be given out before you can save.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
